{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":484218,"name":"John Millard","username":"John_Millard","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/dfb087/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:57:15.566Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484218-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484218-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484218-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484218-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn the Windows Grok Bot desktop app, one existing conversation with my bot “Walter” will not open. The main pane stays empty/dark, then after sign-out/sign-in it shows:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Couldn’t load conversation”\u003cbr\u003e\n“Couldn’t load this conversation. Check your connection and try again.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe sidebar still lists Walter and shows live message previews (including new lines). I can still see the composer (“Message Walter”). The same conversation loads and works fully on mobile. New rooms on the same Windows app work normally.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI signed into Grok Bot with X. Sidebar account name is John Millard.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis does not look like “Can’t reach your computer.” I did not Reset or Recover the Agent Computer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484218-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484218-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot on Windows, signed in (X login). Bot “Walter” and other rooms appear.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the existing main Walter conversation.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eResult: message pane is blank/dark. Sidebar previews for that bot still update. Sending from desktop previously worked; replies showed in the sidebar only.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit via Task Manager (no tray Quit option). Relaunch. Same room still blank.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSign out and sign back in with the same account. Same room now shows “Couldn’t load conversation” with Retry. Retry does nothing.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRename %APPDATA%\\Roaming\\Grok Bot to Grok Bot.bak, relaunch so a fresh Grok Bot folder is created. Same error on that room.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen a new room on desktop: conversation loads and works.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the original Walter thread on mobile: full history and chat work.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484218-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484218-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe existing Walter conversation should load in the desktop message pane the same way it does on mobile, and the same way new rooms already do on this PC. Sidebar previews and the cloud conversation should match the open thread.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484218-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484218-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/4/a/4a3af5e6ce453f85fa0b816f2c8f516b579f688e.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/aAFECEdAfzPsj09uVQNQlWmQbYq.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-09-05 124342.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/4/a/4a3af5e6ce453f85fa0b816f2c8f516b579f688e_2_646x499.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-05 124342.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"aAFECEdAfzPsj09uVQNQlWmQbYq\" width=\"646\" height=\"499\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/4/a/4a3af5e6ce453f85fa0b816f2c8f516b579f688e_2_646x499.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/4/a/4a3af5e6ce453f85fa0b816f2c8f516b579f688e_2_969x748.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/4/a/4a3af5e6ce453f85fa0b816f2c8f516b579f688e_2_1292x998.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"161616\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot 2026-09-05 124342.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1521×1176 79.6 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484218-operating-system-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484218-operating-system-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484218-version-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484218-version-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion: 0.43.0\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease Track: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: win32\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484218-additional-information-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484218-additional-information-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSigned into Grok Bot with X. Sidebar account: John Millard.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBroken room: existing conversation with bot “Walter”.\u003cbr\u003e\nDesktop: sidebar previews update; main pane “Couldn’t load conversation”.\u003cbr\u003e\nMobile: same thread loads and chat works.\u003cbr\u003e\nNew rooms on this Windows app work.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlready tried (no Reset/Recover of Agent Computer):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClose window vs full Task Manager kill of Grok Bot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSign out / sign in\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRetry on the error screen\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRenamed %APPDATA%\\Roaming\\Grok Bot → Grok Bot.bak; app created a new Grok Bot folder; error remains\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease do not reset the Agent Computer unless you confirm it is required. Bots and other conversations are fine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484218-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484218-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-05T20:22:22.822Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170723,"topic_slug":"windows-grok-bot-desktop-can-t-load-an-existing-walter-conversation-sidebar-and-mobile-still-work","display_username":"John Millard","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136354,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/windows-grok-bot-desktop-can-t-load-an-existi